<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  macOS Hardened Runtime entitlements (Developer ID direct download).

  Deliberately minimal. Corvux ships UNSANDBOXED on macOS — the App Sandbox
  would break the corvux-mcp sidecar, sync, and filesystem access (the same
  reason we ship Developer ID direct, not the Mac App Store). So there is NO
  com.apple.security.app-sandbox here.

  The only two entitlements are the device-access pair the in-app WebKit media
  features need under Hardened Runtime (without them the OS denies the request
  on a signed/notarized build even though it works in unsigned dev):
    - audio-input : the voice-memo recorder (getUserMedia audio)
    - camera      : the sync QR-pairing scanner (getUserMedia video)
  Both also require the matching NSMicrophone/NSCamera usage strings — see
  src-tauri/Info.plist.

  Do NOT add com.apple.security.cs.* (allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory
  / disable-library-validation / allow-dyld-environment-variables): JavaScript JIT
  runs in the OS's own sandboxed WebContent process, not the host app, so the host
  needs none of them. Adding them weakens the Hardened Runtime for no reason.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
